# Optional Cloud Functions runtime config for the Nexus Letters models.
#
# These are ALL OPTIONAL. With nothing set, the defaults shown below apply, so
# you do not need any .env file to run the app. firebase-tools loads this
# directory's .env files into the function environment at deploy time, so to
# override a value, copy this file to a real (git-ignored) one and redeploy:
#
#   cp functions/.env.example functions/.env                           # all projects
#   cp functions/.env.example functions/.env.veteran-claims-buddy-dev  # dev only
#
# Uncomment only the lines you want to change. A value takes effect on the next
# `npx -y firebase-tools@latest deploy --only functions --project dev`.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Available model IDs
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model values below are Vertex AI Gemini model IDs. Availability and exact
# IDs change over time and vary by project and region (we call us-central1).
# The authoritative, current list lives here:
#
#   https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/models
#   (per-model IDs: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/models/gemini/2-5-flash
#    and .../2-5-pro — swap the last path segment for other models)
#
# To see what is actually enabled on this project, from the repo root run:
#   gcloud ai models list --region=us-central1 --project=veteran-claims-buddy-dev
#
# Commonly available Gemini text models at the time of writing:
#   gemini-2.5-pro         strongest reasoning, best quality drafting (default draft)
#   gemini-2.5-flash       fast and inexpensive, proven across this app (default interview)
#   gemini-2.5-flash-lite  fastest and cheapest, lighter quality

# Model that phrases the gap-interview questions. Default: gemini-2.5-flash
# NEXUS_INTERVIEW_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Model that drafts the two letters. Default: gemini-2.5-pro
# If gemini-2.5-pro is not enabled on the project, drafting automatically falls
# back to the interview model. Set this to pin flash and skip the failed attempt:
# NEXUS_DRAFT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Sampling temperature for drafting, 0 to 1 (higher = more varied wording, lower
# = more deterministic). Does not affect facts or citations. Default: 0.45
# NEXUS_DRAFT_TEMPERATURE=0.45
